/-!
# Chromatic homotopy theory: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md. This file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned APIs whenever their actual carriers exist.

Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.SymmetricSpectrum` is the point-set category of symmetric
spectra of pointed simplicial sets, without the stable model structure, stable
homotopy groups or a derived smash product. "The stable homotopy category"
below means that missing structure.

The following headline theorems are not statable at the pins:

- Generalized Serre filtration with monodromy and convergence (§3.1): missing
  the stable homotopy category, spectrum-valued fiber local systems and their
  filtered homotopy colimits.
- Nonzero raw KU Tate spectrum and its Euler-inversion calculation (§4.1): missing
  the KU spectrum, its derived completion and the spectral Tate construction.
- Higher semiadditivity of T(n)-local spectra and K(n)-local Morava E-modules,
  their dimension formula and the π-finite fiber comparison (§4.2): missing
  the stable homotopy category, local spectral module categories, 2-periodic
  Morava residue theories and higher Kan-extension norms.
- The sharp connectivity bound m=n+1 in periodic vanishing and suspension–loop
  preservation (§4.3): missing the stable homotopy category, telescopes,
  periodic homotopy groups and finite chromatic localizations.
- The weak-ring height criterion, equating vanishing against a finite
  type-(n+1) spectrum, against Σ∞K(C_p,n+1), against every K(j) with j>n and
  on Σ∞_+ of maps of π-finite spaces that are equivalences on n-th Postnikov
  sections (§4.4): missing the stable homotopy category, Morava K-theories and
  the type of a finite spectrum.
- Faithful full-level spectral Galois extensions TMF[1/N]→TMF(N) for every N≥1
  (§5.1): missing spectral level stacks, E∞ spectral algebras, relative tensor
  and coherent homotopy fixed points.

The higher-height telescope separation theorem, with its fixed-point trace
comparison and BP model theorem, is the separate Part II target specified in
Scope and ownership. It lacks spectral localizations, the BP ring models with
coherent Adams actions, their algebraic K-spectra and cyclotomic coassembly.
The periodic, finite-local, Tate, height, realization and Thom constructions
consumed here retain their supplier ownership in README.md.

Algebraic formal groups and ordinary category-localization predicates do not
provide these spectral carriers. No coefficient identity or arbitrary
Prop-valued replacement states any of these headline theorems.
-/

